WEBVTT

00:14.507 --> 00:15.467
Subaru?

00:18.267 --> 00:19.417
What's wrong?

00:19.957 --> 00:22.107
Just a little nervous.

00:22.107 --> 00:25.117
I mean, considering where 
we're headed, y'know?

00:25.117 --> 00:26.647
Yes, you're right.

00:26.647 --> 00:29.167
Ram and Rem are with us this time,

00:29.167 --> 00:32.767
not to mention Meili and 
our guide, Lady Anastasia.

00:33.497 --> 00:36.247
And I need to keep you safe, too.

00:36.247 --> 00:40.307
Wait, what?! You're counting me 
with the ones who need protecting?!

00:41.477 --> 00:42.817
Oh, dear.

00:43.127 --> 00:47.507
I don't think they like the 
mabeast smell I have on me.

00:47.507 --> 00:49.027
Hey, come on, Joseph!

00:49.027 --> 00:50.547
Let her go!

00:52.897 --> 00:54.157
Good boy.

00:57.117 --> 01:02.267
Stroking the neck like this 
calms most land dragons.

01:02.267 --> 01:03.657
Huh...

01:03.657 --> 01:05.727
Is that true, Patrasche?

01:06.917 --> 01:08.907
Not for that one, I guess.

01:08.907 --> 01:13.677
Big Brother, don't leave me 
alone with that one, all right?

01:14.007 --> 01:16.367
I might just get gobbled up.

01:16.367 --> 01:18.307
Nothing that scary is gonna happen!

01:18.307 --> 01:20.767
Patrasche is a vegetarian!

01:21.217 --> 01:23.607
Subaru. Lady Emilia.

01:24.067 --> 01:26.697
There's something you need 
to know about Ram's body.

01:28.187 --> 01:28.907
Got it.

01:29.347 --> 01:34.677
You can ask Ram herself or Beatrice 
for more details about the regulation.

01:34.677 --> 01:35.367
Don't worry.

01:36.137 --> 01:38.707
We'll do everything we can for Ram.

01:40.777 --> 01:41.667
Master.

01:42.427 --> 01:45.547
Both ladies are ready to go now.

01:45.847 --> 01:47.447
Good work.

01:47.447 --> 01:51.067
Ram, do take care during your travels.

01:51.067 --> 01:54.007
Thank you for granting my selfish request.

01:54.557 --> 01:58.227
I will not fail to return with 
results that meet your expectations.

01:58.827 --> 02:00.907
Subaru... sir...

02:00.907 --> 02:01.937
Be careful.

02:02.367 --> 02:03.667
I will.

02:03.667 --> 02:06.777
Petra and Frederica, hold down 
the fort while we're gone.

02:07.847 --> 02:08.857
We will!

02:09.367 --> 02:10.947
Of course.

02:14.627 --> 02:15.367
Right!

02:15.737 --> 02:19.777
We're off to the Auguria Dunes!

04:12.557 --> 04:13.857
What'll it be?

04:14.327 --> 04:15.387
Milk.

04:16.557 --> 04:18.167
And make it cold.

04:18.167 --> 04:19.297
Milk.

04:19.297 --> 04:20.697
Make mine hot.

04:22.247 --> 04:25.207
Doesn't look like business 
is exactly booming here.

04:25.847 --> 04:28.677
Not a lot of customers
during the sand time?

04:28.677 --> 04:32.797
Yeah. And this town doesn't see 
a lot of outsiders as it is.

04:33.387 --> 04:39.007
So what are you two doing in 
Mirula during the sand time?

04:39.007 --> 04:41.927
I'll tell you. We're going 
to conquer the Auguria Dunes!

04:44.167 --> 04:45.727
Let me give you some advice.

04:46.287 --> 04:47.557
Go home before you die.

04:47.557 --> 04:48.947
I can't do that.

04:49.577 --> 04:52.227
There are times when you just 
can't back down, you know?

04:57.787 --> 04:58.817
In 400 years,

04:59.547 --> 05:02.787
no one has managed to reach that tower.

05:02.787 --> 05:06.237
The dunes are full of mabeasts 
and the witch's miasma.

05:06.817 --> 05:10.457
You can walk forever and never get any 
closer to that tower in the distance.

05:10.457 --> 05:12.337
You'll be lucky if you make it back alive.

05:12.337 --> 05:15.297
Most who've tried are still out 
there in the sand, asleep forever.

05:16.807 --> 05:20.427
Take my advice and don't do anything dumb—

05:19.147 --> 05:20.427
I'm sorry.

05:21.207 --> 05:25.427
I can tell you're deeply concerned for us.

05:26.567 --> 05:30.127
No. I'm just sick of seeing

05:30.127 --> 05:34.237
young, careless folks like you 
end up the same way every time.

05:36.657 --> 05:37.947
Thank you for the drinks.

05:38.697 --> 05:41.517
And thank you for telling
us all that, too.

05:41.517 --> 05:44.017
You've been a big help. Later.

05:53.087 --> 05:55.667
For the past year or so...

05:56.437 --> 06:00.257
folks have been seeing birds 
flying over the dunes.

06:00.957 --> 06:07.477
People who've seen 'em say they're 
always heading toward that tower.

06:07.477 --> 06:11.857
So if you do get lost, look for a bird.

06:11.857 --> 06:15.187
If you're lucky, it might
show you the way.

06:16.027 --> 06:16.897
Mister...

06:17.727 --> 06:21.907
Then again, if you're already lost 
out there with nowhere to turn,

06:21.907 --> 06:24.367
you've clearly got the
worst luck imaginable.

06:25.247 --> 06:26.827
The Pleiades Watchtower.

06:27.327 --> 06:30.667
The tower of the sage with a history, huh?

06:37.757 --> 06:39.897
How have your spirits 
been since that happened?

06:39.897 --> 06:41.317
Nothing has changed.

06:41.317 --> 06:45.097
They stay by my side, 
but they seem perplexed.

06:46.007 --> 06:49.277
My Divine Protection of Guiding 
Spirits seems to be intact.

06:49.277 --> 06:54.177
They seem unsure why they find 
it difficult to leave my side.

06:54.177 --> 06:58.357
So I guess even though they forgot 
you, the contract isn't broken.

07:00.167 --> 07:01.497
Which means, right now,

07:01.497 --> 07:04.857
I can only fulfill my duty as 
a knight with my swordsmanship.

07:05.607 --> 07:07.617
It's a fact that without my spirit arts,

07:07.617 --> 07:10.567
my capacity has dropped significantly.

07:12.927 --> 07:15.957
Why do you appear even
more vexed than I am?

07:15.957 --> 07:18.477
Who said I was?! Don't go 
saying whatever you want!

07:18.477 --> 07:20.857
Why would I be
vexed because you're weaker?!

07:20.857 --> 07:22.427
Who told you that?!

07:25.337 --> 07:29.457
You are less suited to keeping 
secrets than I realized.

07:29.457 --> 07:32.067
Perhaps it's because I've been 
traveling with you for a while,

07:32.067 --> 07:34.147
but I feel as though I've 
come to understand you.

07:34.147 --> 07:36.407
Well, same here!

07:36.407 --> 07:38.627
If this keeps up and nothing else happens,

07:38.627 --> 07:41.357
I'm gonna be an authority on you 
by the time we reach the tower.

07:41.697 --> 07:43.467
Not to worry.

07:43.467 --> 07:46.647
Excluding myself, you are 
already undeniably the one

07:46.647 --> 07:49.197
who knows me better than
anyone in the world.

07:49.497 --> 07:53.077
Damn it, I got myself stuck 
with a title I never wanted!

07:54.167 --> 07:55.457
Subaru!

07:55.457 --> 07:58.087
You can't keep playing 
around forever, I suppose.

07:58.647 --> 08:01.667
The sand time is about to start.

08:17.127 --> 08:18.807
Hang in there, Patrasche!

08:18.807 --> 08:20.237
You, too, Joseph!

08:21.597 --> 08:23.127
We've got wind and miasma,

08:23.127 --> 08:25.297
and we need to watch out for mabeasts, too!

08:25.297 --> 08:29.947
And to make sure we don't lose sight 
of the tower and get lost, I suppose.

08:30.397 --> 08:34.717
I dunno, I feel like it'd be harder 
to lose sight of that thing.

08:34.717 --> 08:37.037
Betty agrees with you,

08:37.037 --> 08:39.877
but anything can happen here, I suppose.

08:40.387 --> 08:44.217
The fact that no one has ever 
made it there proves it.

08:44.217 --> 08:45.597
True.

08:46.937 --> 08:48.577
Lady Anastasia?

08:49.917 --> 08:51.097
What's goin' on?

08:51.097 --> 08:54.217
You're sure we just need 
to keep going straight?

08:54.217 --> 08:57.967
Aw, Natsuki, why're ya
so suspicious of me?

08:58.567 --> 09:00.697
We're in the same boat here.

09:00.697 --> 09:02.227
You can trust me.

09:02.227 --> 09:06.607
Trusting a fox is easier 
said than done, I suppose.

09:07.367 --> 09:10.057
Oh? You told her, Natsuki?

09:10.057 --> 09:13.737
Well, <i>Lady Anastasia</i> wouldn't 
particularly care, right?

09:13.737 --> 09:15.367
Ya got that right, Natsuki!

09:15.867 --> 09:18.087
You needn't worry.

09:18.087 --> 09:19.747
I will keep my promise.

09:23.017 --> 09:26.297
And what about you, Meili? 
You doing your job?

09:26.297 --> 09:30.857
We haven't run into a single mabeast 
since we entered the dunes, have we?

09:30.857 --> 09:33.877
What? That's because of you?

09:33.877 --> 09:36.217
Oh, you have to ask?

09:36.217 --> 09:40.017
Then I'll show you just how 
much you should appreciate me.

09:51.777 --> 09:53.887
There! All done!

09:58.287 --> 09:59.747
What was...

09:59.747 --> 10:02.097
It was a sandworm.

10:02.097 --> 10:05.627
I don't recall any records 
of one that large, though.

10:05.927 --> 10:10.757
Well? Starting to see me 
in a different light now?

10:47.507 --> 10:51.757
Man, I'm dying to get out of 
these dunes and into a bathtub!

10:52.077 --> 10:53.927
I'm with ya there.

10:53.927 --> 10:57.507
But you two must have 
realized it by now, right?

10:57.507 --> 10:59.507
Yeah, I get it.

10:59.507 --> 11:02.797
We've been heading straight 
for it all this time...

11:02.797 --> 11:04.817
But we aren't getting 
any closer to the tower.

11:05.187 --> 11:09.447
This must be why Reinhard 
never made it there.

11:09.447 --> 11:11.527
The space around here is warped.

11:11.867 --> 11:13.647
The space is warped?

11:13.647 --> 11:17.407
Basically, it seems like the dunes 
and the tower are connected,

11:17.407 --> 11:19.187
but they're not.

11:19.667 --> 11:24.707
We might actually just be 
runnin' around in circles.

11:24.707 --> 11:29.517
And that's why the Auguria 
Dunes are so dangerous?

11:29.517 --> 11:30.697
It makes sense.

11:30.697 --> 11:34.227
So are we also gonna be overpowered 
by the distortion in space

11:34.227 --> 11:35.797
that's sunk so many adventurers?

11:35.797 --> 11:41.317
That's why I volunteered to guide 
y'all to the Pleiades Watchtower.

11:41.317 --> 11:43.597
When a merchant heads out
to make a purchase,

11:43.597 --> 11:45.897
they're headin' out to win.

11:46.387 --> 11:50.737
Are you saying you can 
see a path to the tower?

11:50.737 --> 11:53.397
The sand time, when the wind picks up,

11:53.397 --> 11:56.777
is the recoil from space twistin' 
and returnin' to normal.

11:56.777 --> 11:59.367
In other words, the periods 
between the sand times

11:59.367 --> 12:01.997
are when the distortion's lettin' up.

12:02.807 --> 12:04.527
And through those cracks

12:04.527 --> 12:07.207
is the real sea of sand that's 
connected to the tower.

12:07.577 --> 12:09.727
The real sea of sand...

12:09.727 --> 12:16.047
And the one who's gonna play the vital 
role of findin' those cracks is...

12:28.277 --> 12:31.857
We need your clairvoyance to see 
through the eyes of mabeasts.

12:32.557 --> 12:35.547
If there are mabeasts that stay 
active during the sand time,

12:35.547 --> 12:38.787
there must be some that come across 
the cracks in space somewhere.

12:36.947 --> 12:38.787
A bit more to the north.

12:38.787 --> 12:40.537
Is it a sandworm?

12:40.867 --> 12:45.427
And to find them, we have 
Meili locate the mabeasts

12:45.427 --> 12:47.247
and tell Miss Ram where they are.

12:49.397 --> 12:50.087
It's no use.

12:50.837 --> 12:52.487
I've lost the connection.

12:56.127 --> 12:59.157
Subaru, we can't put Ram through any more.

12:59.157 --> 13:00.187
Lady Emilia.

13:01.207 --> 13:03.577
There is no one else suited to this.

13:03.577 --> 13:05.937
This is a job only I can do.

13:07.727 --> 13:10.687
Meili, you can leave out the 
mabeasts that are underground.

13:11.297 --> 13:14.097
There's no point when all I can see is sand.

13:14.097 --> 13:16.717
I can't tell them apart that well.

13:16.717 --> 13:20.267
Maybe you should stop giving 
up on them right away?

13:20.267 --> 13:23.157
I don't think the idea in itself is wrong.

13:23.447 --> 13:26.777
It's just a matter of meetin' 
the right mabeast, I guess.

13:26.777 --> 13:30.767
If we're calling this a contest of luck, 
we're at a huge disadvantage.

13:34.607 --> 13:35.927
A bird?

13:35.927 --> 13:38.867
Can't believe a bird would 
wanna fly through <i>this</i> sky.

13:38.867 --> 13:39.677
A bird?

13:41.797 --> 13:42.967
Natsuki?

13:47.167 --> 13:48.747
Subaru! Is there a bird?

13:48.747 --> 13:49.877
Yeah!

13:49.877 --> 13:52.697
Ram, can you see through a bird's eyes?

13:52.697 --> 13:53.647
What do you mean?

13:54.007 --> 13:55.777
Those birds are the key!

14:05.697 --> 14:06.547
I've got it!

14:06.547 --> 14:07.787
Yes!

14:11.907 --> 14:14.347
This time, we're gonna make 
it through the sand time!

14:14.347 --> 14:15.487
Let's go!

14:31.447 --> 14:33.857
Straight. Keep going straight.

14:35.857 --> 14:37.757
<i>Please get us out!</i>

14:37.757 --> 14:40.777
<i>I don't want to put them through any more!</i>

14:41.347 --> 14:42.537
<i>Please!</i>

14:55.727 --> 14:57.687
We did it! We're out!

14:57.687 --> 14:59.667
We did it! We did it!

14:59.057 --> 15:02.617
Hey! Quit screaming in my ears, I suppose!

15:02.617 --> 15:04.597
Aw, no need to put on airs!

15:04.597 --> 15:05.827
Show some joy!

15:05.827 --> 15:08.017
Come on! Banzai!

15:08.017 --> 15:09.847
Grr, I say.

15:09.847 --> 15:12.227
Banzai... I suppose.

15:12.537 --> 15:15.357
Look at that! It's proof 
we've made it to a new stage!

15:15.797 --> 15:18.447
The dunes turned into an 
endless field of flowers...

15:19.547 --> 15:22.737
An endless field of... flowers?

15:24.067 --> 15:25.487
They're oiran bears.

15:31.057 --> 15:32.497
Subaru, what happened?

15:32.497 --> 15:34.747
Ram's clairvoyance suddenly—

15:33.697 --> 15:34.747
Stop.

15:35.327 --> 15:37.457
Emilia-tan, stay calm.

15:37.927 --> 15:39.167
Keep quiet.

15:44.727 --> 15:47.857
Shh. Don't move.

16:10.747 --> 16:11.447
No!

16:23.057 --> 16:24.527
Run!

16:27.717 --> 16:30.097
They're coming! They're coming!
They're coming! They're coming!

16:30.097 --> 16:33.347
Hah! Yah! There! Take that!

16:33.347 --> 16:35.107
Take a whole bunch of them!

16:35.987 --> 16:38.777
Yeah! That's my Emilia-tan!

16:38.777 --> 16:41.647
Barusu, if you don't want to die, 
make that thing run for all it's worth!

16:41.647 --> 16:43.737
Of course I—wait, Ram?!

16:50.477 --> 16:54.247
I cannot allow Lady Emilia 
to shoulder all the work.

16:54.247 --> 16:55.997
Damn! I can't let him beat me!

16:56.337 --> 16:57.647
Beako, you ready?!

16:57.647 --> 16:59.007
Of course I am!

16:59.007 --> 17:02.297
It's you who'd better not 
run out of gas, I suppose!

17:02.677 --> 17:03.587
Minya!

17:09.887 --> 17:12.347
Go, sandworm!

17:12.347 --> 17:15.307
Crush 'em all!

17:18.267 --> 17:19.807
We're almost there!

17:19.807 --> 17:22.437
We just gotta charge straight 
for the watchtower!

17:24.477 --> 17:25.147
What—

17:31.427 --> 17:31.987
<i>Huh?</i>

17:33.617 --> 17:35.767
<i>I died? And went back?</i>

17:35.767 --> 17:36.867
<i>Why? When?!</i>

17:37.377 --> 17:38.587
<i>What happened?!</i>

17:38.587 --> 17:40.207
<i>How did I die?!</i>

17:40.207 --> 17:42.837
<i>Shit, shit, shit, shi—</i>

17:46.627 --> 17:48.947
No! Juli—

17:52.117 --> 17:54.967
Damn it! Run! Run! Run! Run! Run!

17:54.967 --> 17:57.847
Hah! Yah! There! Take that!

17:57.847 --> 17:59.447
Subaru!

17:59.447 --> 18:00.357
Beatrice...

18:02.137 --> 18:02.977
Minya!

18:07.267 --> 18:08.867
I've got something for you!

18:08.867 --> 18:10.987
Sandworm!

18:14.407 --> 18:16.407
Go!

18:17.727 --> 18:21.417
Crap! This is going exactly 
the same way as before!

18:21.417 --> 18:24.567
Barusu, if you don't want to die, 
make that thing run for all it's worth!

18:24.567 --> 18:27.837
Ram! Don't head for the tower! 
We gotta find another route!

18:27.837 --> 18:29.407
What are you saying?!

18:29.407 --> 18:31.797
It's a straight line, and every 
other path is full of mabeasts!

18:31.797 --> 18:33.297
We can't go straight to it!

18:33.297 --> 18:35.447
We have to change directions!

18:36.087 --> 18:36.767
Ram!

18:36.767 --> 18:38.777
Do as Subaru says!

18:38.777 --> 18:42.647
He would never just blurt out 
something silly without a reason!

18:42.647 --> 18:45.687
Barusu speaks nonsense and 
falsehoods on a daily basis!

18:46.007 --> 18:50.567
He would never just blurt out something 
silly for no reason when we're in danger!

18:50.567 --> 18:53.737
Thanks for the rephrase!

18:57.317 --> 18:59.747
You two up top, don't get shaken off!

19:11.497 --> 19:13.337
Dodge!

19:26.237 --> 19:27.437
That was close.

19:28.727 --> 19:30.737
Subaru, we messed up!

19:30.737 --> 19:31.397
Huh?

19:31.847 --> 19:34.767
We got separated from Emilia's 
carriage, I suppose!

19:34.767 --> 19:36.407
It's just you and Betty!

19:36.407 --> 19:37.927
What?!

19:37.927 --> 19:41.537
Damn it, beating that bastard 
Regulus was easier than this!

19:41.537 --> 19:44.137
No time for complaining, I suppose!

19:44.137 --> 19:45.367
We have to find—

19:45.367 --> 19:46.377
I know!

19:46.377 --> 19:48.707
I'm thinking!

19:56.247 --> 19:57.817
<i>What... just...</i>

20:01.807 --> 20:03.597
Subaru!

20:04.037 --> 20:06.477
Subaru! Subaru!

20:08.357 --> 20:10.737
No! You can't die!

20:10.737 --> 20:12.757
Don't die!

20:12.757 --> 20:14.997
Don't leave me alone...

20:14.997 --> 20:16.317
Don't!

20:16.317 --> 20:19.267
Don't leave Betty behind...

20:19.267 --> 20:20.197
Suba—

20:48.137 --> 20:51.527
<i>The first and second death were both...</i>

21:05.487 --> 21:07.577
Beako, I love you.

21:07.577 --> 21:07.997
Huh?

21:09.207 --> 21:12.477
<i>Invisible Providence!</i>

21:19.337 --> 21:20.137
Good boy.

21:36.007 --> 21:39.127
There's something I want to ask you guys.

21:39.127 --> 21:41.947
Did anyone else see a flash of 
light coming from the tower?

21:41.947 --> 21:43.587
A light from the tower?

21:43.587 --> 21:44.497
Yeah.

21:44.897 --> 21:47.687
What do you think this light was?

21:47.687 --> 21:51.607
I... think it's something dangerous.

21:51.607 --> 21:53.847
Definitely not friendly, at least.

21:53.847 --> 21:54.877
Based only on a hunch?

21:54.877 --> 21:58.227
Well... yeah.

21:58.227 --> 21:59.937
I see. That's troubling.

21:59.937 --> 22:01.967
It's just a hunch! You believe me?

22:02.427 --> 22:04.307
It's <i>your</i> hunch.

22:04.307 --> 22:06.227
So I think it's worth worrying about.

22:08.087 --> 22:09.197
Oh...

22:10.217 --> 22:10.857
Ram?

22:12.937 --> 22:14.107
It's looking...

22:15.217 --> 22:16.417
at Barusu?

22:21.237 --> 22:22.697
I won't let you!

22:39.337 --> 22:40.297
A needle?

22:40.297 --> 22:42.257
Barusu! Another one's coming!

22:42.257 --> 22:44.057
Beako, you ready?!

22:44.057 --> 22:45.217
Obviously!

22:47.047 --> 22:48.327
E-M-T!

22:48.327 --> 22:49.847
I suppose!

22:57.677 --> 22:58.577
This is...

22:58.577 --> 23:01.847
Absolute nullification magic, E-M-T.

23:01.847 --> 23:06.147
All magic loses its effect 
within this field.

23:06.147 --> 23:08.787
The catch is... it doesn't last long.

23:08.787 --> 23:09.537
What?!

23:09.537 --> 23:11.307
We messed up!

23:11.307 --> 23:14.697
E-M-T is making the distortion 
in space come undone!

23:14.697 --> 23:19.127
I get it! The sand time works the 
same way as Beako's Door Crossing!

23:37.477 --> 23:38.957
I found you.

23:37.477 --> 23:40.067
<b>Overcome Sand Time</b>
